1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:44,200
I don't buy it.

3
00:01:44,280 --> 00:01:45,360
Nothing's wrong?

4
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:48,840
Then why did you end up in the hospital
and take a whole day of sick leave?

5
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:51,760
I warned you before not to travel so much.

6
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,000
See what happened?

7
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:56,440
When did you ever warn me?
You definitely didn't.

8
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:58,680
Because you knew I had a fire in my belly.

9
00:01:58,760 --> 00:01:59,840
I just couldn't accept it.

10
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:03,160
You beat me to project manager
so much earlier.

11
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:05,480
Even if you took it over halfway through.

12
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:09,160
Show some respect
in front of your superior.

13
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:11,320
Okay, okay, boss.

14
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,400
Don't worry. I definitely
won't push myself that hard anymore.

15
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:14,400
If I end up in the hospital again,

16
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,520
I'll drink ten bottles
of your nourishing soup.

17
00:02:17,440 --> 00:02:18,600
Let's talk business.

18
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:20,520
Once you're done with your project,

19
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,520
do you want to help me keep an eye
on the actuarial side?

20
00:02:23,280 --> 00:02:24,240
I'll pass.

21
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,240
I want to take it easy next week.

22
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:27,920
Once things wrap up
with the IT Department,

23
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,920
I'll cut back on overtime
and spend more time with him.

24
00:02:30,840 --> 00:02:32,080
You're not working overtime?

25
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:39,480
I feel like I really need to rethink
the meaning of my life.

26
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:43,960
The meaning of life?

27
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:45,640
Don't tell me you're gonna--

28
00:02:49,520 --> 00:02:52,080
Getting sick actually
changed you a bit, huh?

29
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,880
If you wanna say I got prettier,
just say it.

30
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:57,160
Let me tell you, 12 hours of sleep
works better than any cosmetic procedure.

31
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,280
Look at those dark circles of yours…

32
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:00,480
Those are natural.

33
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:12,320
What's wrong? You two got into it again?

34
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,360
What is wrong with Shen Jin?

35
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,880
I just saw him
posting lovey-dovey stuff with Lin

36
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,600
on Moments a couple of days ago.

37
00:03:29,680 --> 00:03:31,440
I'll have Lin tear him a new one.

38
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:33,080
What good would that do?

39
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,720
Actually, Zhao Heng was right.

40
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:40,360
I think I've been avoiding it.

41
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,720
I don't think

42
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,720
I've ever really treated him
like a real boyfriend.

43
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:46,680
You know what the problem is, so fix it.

44
00:03:46,760 --> 00:03:47,880
It's not that easy.

45
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:54,040
You watched him scheme
step by step to win me over.

46
00:03:54,120 --> 00:03:54,960
Yeah.

47
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:56,360
He treats me really well.

48
00:03:56,440 --> 00:04:00,120
But when he suddenly goes cold on me,
I get scared he's gaslighting me.

49
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:02,720
If I give in this time, what if one day

50
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:04,400
he gets stronger

51
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:06,040
and decides he won't put up
with my bad temper anymore?

52
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,360
What do I do then?

53
00:04:08,360 --> 00:04:09,480
And my dad…

54
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,960
My dad won't give me anything.

55
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:12,720
He's leaving it all to my brother.
What am I supposed to do?

56
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:17,720
I get it.

57
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:22,600
At the end of the day, you're just scared
you'll lose in this relationship.

58
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:25,680
You're actually nowhere near
as confident as you pretend to be.

59
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:27,560
-That's not it.
-Not it?

60
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:29,320
-No.
-Okay then.

61
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,040
Then just keep giving him
the cold shoulder like before.

62
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:33,200
But what if he doesn't come to me anymore?

63
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:36,000
Let him go, of course.
There are plenty of men out there.

64
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:37,520
-No.
-Why not?

65
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,120
I like him. I can't be without--

66
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:47,760
Missy, stop pretending you're tough.

67
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:50,800
Since you like him,
just be firm and brave.

68
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,720
Love isn't strategic consulting.

69
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,440
You don't need to plan every move.

70
00:04:54,520 --> 00:04:56,800
Yeah, no one knows what the future holds.

71
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:58,000
But at least enjoy the present.

72
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:08,120
Forget it. Just do whatever.

73
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:10,440
Anyway, there are tons
of rich, pretty girls out there.

74
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:12,280
After he finishes the Celestial project,

75
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:15,040
he can take that track record
to the next company and find someone new.

76
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,720
I think that works too.

77
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:25,440
It's me. Come to the front desk right now.

78
00:05:25,520 --> 00:05:26,520
I need to talk to you.

79
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,360
-Come with me.
-Where to?

80
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:33,280
To meet clients.

81
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:42,080
International Equestrian Culture Week?

82
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:43,560
What are clients doing here?

83
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:51,400
‎-Isn't that one my horse?
‎-Yes, you are right.

84
00:05:52,920 --> 00:05:54,560
-Dad!
-Look, that one's picking up.

85
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,680
Hello, Mr. Liu, Mr. Wang.

86
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:03,200
Nana's getting prettier and prettier.

87
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,520
Such a striking presence.

88
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:06,800
What are you doing here?

89
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,200
Siwei sponsored so many great events.

90
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:11,000
Of course, I had to come check it out.

91
00:06:11,520 --> 00:06:14,840
Oh, let me introduce you
to my boyfriend, Zhao Heng.

92
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:16,440
He's also my colleague at Maxmise.

93
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:20,120
Nana's got good taste.

94
00:06:20,720 --> 00:06:22,280
Really good. Not bad at all.

95
00:06:23,080 --> 00:06:24,120
Say hi.

96
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:28,760
-Hi, Mr. Bu.
-Hello.

97
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,360
Hello, Mr. Liu, Mr. Wang.

98
00:06:31,720 --> 00:06:34,080
I'll go say hi to the other elders.

99
00:06:36,840 --> 00:06:38,080
Nana…

100
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:39,480
Look at Nana's boyfriend.

101
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,760
He's actually pretty great.

102
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:43,400
Nice. Nice.

103
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:51,360
Weren't you forcing me to choose?

104
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:52,880
Now I've chosen.

105
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:56,120
I just told my dad and all his friends
that you're my boyfriend.

106
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:58,440
-There's no backing out now.
-Wait, Tianna--

107
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:00,160
Save it. Let me tell you.

108
00:07:00,240 --> 00:07:02,280
Right now, my dad cares
too much about his precious image

109
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,640
to come running out and yell at me.

110
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:05,640
But after this,
I'm definitely in for a storm.

111
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,520
Weren't you determined
to be the ultimate schemer?

112
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:11,280
Then you must have all kinds of plans
for dealing with my dad.

113
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,920
Put them together
and send them over to me.

114
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,160
I'm heading back to Celestial.

115
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:32,080
What are you doing?

116
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,520
Happy wife, happy life.

117
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:39,080
I'm really happy right now.

118
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:42,800
Because you must love me so much
to say all that in front of your dad.

119
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:45,240
From what I know,
you're not usually that bold.

120
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:47,160
Stop talking nonsense. What do you know?

121
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:50,280
I just know.

122
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:17,160
<i>Yuanzhou Gallery is suspected</i>

123
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:19,160
<i>of colluding with overseas platforms</i>
<i>in a rat-trading scheme.</i>

124
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,360
<i>Market value has plunged nearly 60%.</i>

125
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:21,560
-<i>Back up!</i>
-<i>Regulators</i>

126
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,200
-<i>have moved in to investigate on site.</i>
-<i>Step back!</i>

127
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,120
<i>Back up!</i>

128
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,080
<i>Step back.</i>

129
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,680
<i>Don't push!</i>

130
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:27,840
<i>Give us an answer!</i>

131
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:30,960
Xinzhi!

132
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,679
Come quick!

133
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,039
What's wrong?

134
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:36,480
You guys move fast.

135
00:08:36,559 --> 00:08:38,440
-I looked away for a few days,
-<i>Step back!</i>

136
00:08:38,520 --> 00:08:39,559
and it's already come to this?

137
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:41,880
-<i>Step back!</i>
-<i>Pay up!</i>

138
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,760
While you were wrapping up
the Celestial project,

139
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:45,000
-Du and I were busy with this.
-<i>Please comment on the situation!</i>

140
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:47,240
Once the first domino falls,

141
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:48,560
the rest will follow.

142
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,080
He had it coming.

143
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:58,280
Karma never misses.

144
00:08:58,880 --> 00:09:01,200
He's been reaching out
to everyone he can lately.

145
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:03,920
I only went on that business trip
because I didn't want to see him.

146
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:09,920
You sly fox.

147
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:15,280
<i>Move aside! Step back!</i>

148
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:17,920
<i>Don't push. Step back.</i>

149
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:19,640
Say it again.

150
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,960
I like hearing it.

151
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,640
You bit me.

152
00:09:33,240 --> 00:09:34,920
I like hearing that too.

153
00:10:20,400 --> 00:10:21,320
Mom.

154
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:26,960
Mrs. Bu. Hello.

155
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:28,040
I brought you your favorite

156
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,560
-Zhang's Crispy Pastries.
-Right.

157
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:31,720
Come to the table.
The food's getting cold.

158
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:38,120
Tianna, where's the toy you brought me?

159
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:42,320
-Right here.
-Say thank you to Zhao Heng.

160
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:45,080
Wrong. It's Brother-in-Law Zhao.

161
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,360
Let me ask you, where's Dad?

162
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:53,240
Was he mad? Did he lose his temper?

163
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:58,400
He just fought with Mom and smashed a cup.

164
00:10:58,960 --> 00:11:00,080
It's fine. We'll play it by ear.

165
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:01,080
Dad… Dad.

166
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:03,400
Jie, stop playing. Come eat.

167
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:04,480
‎Okay.

168
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,920
What's going on? The silent treatment?

169
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:13,360
It's fine.

170
00:11:25,800 --> 00:11:26,880
Eat.

171
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:49,200
Eat up.

172
00:11:57,680 --> 00:12:01,200
-Dad. Mom.
-No talking at meals.

173
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:04,040
Don't forget the rules
your mom taught you.

174
00:12:04,120 --> 00:12:06,240
After all,
that's the Bu family upbringing.

175
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:08,160
Especially with an outsider here.

176
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:23,040
Mom.

177
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:24,880
I want to go to the bathroom.

178
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:27,920
Take him, ma'am.

179
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,080
No. Mom, I want you to take me.

180
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:34,240
Go on. Take him.

181
00:12:34,320 --> 00:12:35,320
Okay.

182
00:12:36,520 --> 00:12:37,800
I'll take him.

183
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:45,080
You brat.

184
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:50,280
Let's go.

185
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,120
I'm done eating.

186
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:04,600
Dad!

187
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:08,640
I brought a whole living,
breathing person home.

188
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:10,600
You can't just act like you don't see him.

189
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:12,880
I see him.

190
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,480
What else do you expect from me?

191
00:13:14,560 --> 00:13:15,960
He's my boyfriend!

192
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:17,040
Enough.

193
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:22,680
Tianna, how you define your relationship
is your own business.

194
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:23,600
You're all grown up.

195
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:26,160
Your mom and I
respect you unconditionally.

196
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:27,320
Do whatever you want.

197
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:30,040
I'm pregnant!

198
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,120
Are you gonna stay indifferent
after hearing that too?

199
00:13:38,080 --> 00:13:38,960
You're not lying to me, are you?

200
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:40,920
I'm not. It's been three months!

201
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:44,360
Have you no shame?

202
00:13:45,520 --> 00:13:46,840
Are you okay?

203
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:50,400
What are you doing, Dad?

204
00:13:50,480 --> 00:13:51,880
I'm fine. It's alright.

205
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:57,120
Mr. Bu, she's just saying that
out of spite.

206
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,360
We haven't reached that point yet.

207
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:00,920
Don't worry.

208
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:12,200
It's okay.

209
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,320
I know you definitely don't like me,

210
00:14:17,400 --> 00:14:18,680
but considering that slap I just took,

211
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:22,160
could you please spare me three minutes

212
00:14:22,760 --> 00:14:23,840
to hear me out?

213
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:29,840
Speak.

214
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:32,840
It's fine.

215
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:39,560
I know why you allowed me
at the table earlier.

216
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:42,360
And I know…

217
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:46,760
why you gave me the silent treatment.

218
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:49,360
Because you know perfectly well

219
00:14:49,440 --> 00:14:51,360
that forcing us apart…

220
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,400
would only trigger Tianna's rebellion.

221
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:59,320
Who knows, we might
end up even more inseparable.

222
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:04,400
But the cold shoulder
is a whole different game.

223
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:08,240
You know I'll be stewing with frustration.

224
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:09,960
And once the honeymoon phase fades,

225
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:12,280
you figure a punk like me,

226
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:14,120
with his pride bruised,

227
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:16,560
would end up in a huge fight with Tianna.

228
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:20,760
Is that slick tongue of yours
how you won Tianna over?

229
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:23,760
Plus this face and my brain.

230
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:27,680
You might not know this,

231
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:30,400
but Tianna and I
have actually talked a lot.

232
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:32,360
I know what you want.

233
00:15:35,560 --> 00:15:36,480
A legacy that lasts forever, right?

234
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:41,040
The fact that I can work alongside Tianna
already proves what I'm capable of.

235
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:44,000
If you're really not sure Tianna
can handle the company on her own,

236
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:47,040
then would bringing me
into the picture boost the odds?

237
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:56,160
And I know what you're worried about.

238
00:15:57,360 --> 00:15:58,760
I can sign a notarized agreement with you.

239
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:00,600
I promise

240
00:16:01,160 --> 00:16:04,880
that I'll never, directly or indirectly,
hold any equity in Siwei Group.

241
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:06,920
And…

242
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:09,920
if Tianna and I ever break up…

243
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:15,280
I'll lose all management
authority immediately.

244
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:26,560
After all, passion is fleeting,

245
00:16:26,640 --> 00:16:27,800
but interests are forever.

246
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:30,520
As long as I'm working toward
my own future,

247
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:32,000
I'll always love her.

248
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:36,360
What do you think?

249
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:39,200
Dad.

250
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:51,960
Tianna, come play with me.

251
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:53,920
Stop it.

252
00:16:54,640 --> 00:16:56,120
I'll join you guys in a bit. Okay?

253
00:16:56,200 --> 00:16:57,600
Even better!

254
00:16:58,240 --> 00:16:59,840
Jie, quit messing around.

255
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,160
Come with me.

256
00:17:04,160 --> 00:17:05,200
A quick word with you.

257
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:47,840
Does it hurt?

258
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:49,840
It's okay.

259
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:53,600
So, how would you rate
my performance today?

260
00:17:57,120 --> 00:17:59,600
What's wrong? Not happy?

261
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:03,400
I know. It's definitely
because of what I said to your dad.

262
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,120
He's a businessman.

263
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:07,920
The only way he'd actually listen to me

264
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,360
was if I talked to him
in terms of pros and cons.

265
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,960
How much do you love me for me,

266
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:17,280
and how much for what I can give you?

267
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:22,320
You, 70%. The benefits, 30%.

268
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:25,640
Not bad.

269
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:27,840
At least it's not 50-50 or 60-40.

270
00:18:29,120 --> 00:18:30,560
Come on.

271
00:18:30,640 --> 00:18:32,920
I won't repeat
all those sweet things to you.

272
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:38,160
I want us to work together
to turn whatever benefits you bring

273
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,960
into our shared benefits.

274
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,280
Don't let me down.

275
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,280
Got it.

276
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:09,880
My work is pretty much done here.

277
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:11,960
I won't go to Celestial today.

278
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:14,840
I'll give you and Zhao Heng
some alone time.

279
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:19,440
Miss Xu. You have to help me.

280
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,280
The bank pulled my loan approval.

281
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:23,120
Mr. Deng says the earn-out clause
has been triggered.

282
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:24,200
He wants me to sell

283
00:19:24,280 --> 00:19:26,440
-all my shares per the agreement.
-Bye.

284
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:28,640
Richard's gone off the grid.

285
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,440
You're the only one who can help me now.

286
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:32,360
You brokered the funding

287
00:19:32,440 --> 00:19:33,720
for Yuanzhou and Morse.

288
00:19:33,800 --> 00:19:36,360
So, you have to ask Mr. Deng

289
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:38,280
-to give me more time.
-Sorry.

290
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:40,160
I only know how to broker deals.

291
00:19:40,240 --> 00:19:41,880
Don't know anything
about what comes after.

292
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:43,280
You should just talk to Mr. Deng.

293
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:45,200
Sorry, I have to go.

294
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:51,400
Walk out that door,
and I swear I'll ruin your face.

295
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:02,200
I'm not that stupid.

296
00:20:02,280 --> 00:20:04,920
At this point, I know

297
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:08,200
you and Ye Xinzhi teamed up
to set a trap for me.

298
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:10,680
He knows me. Tell him to come see me.

299
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:14,800
Otherwise, if I'm pushed to the edge,
no one gets off easy.

300
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:28,560
Trying to add intentional assault

301
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:30,120
to your financial crimes, are you?

302
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:33,840
Then you won't be the only one going down.

303
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:35,800
Your kid goes down with you.

304
00:20:49,040 --> 00:20:50,440
Are you trying to push me over the edge?

305
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:09,960
‎YE XINZHI

306
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:12,520
<i>Du said Wen Ruosen came to C&amp;C</i>
<i>looking for me.</i>

307
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:15,160
<i>If he comes to you too, bring him to me.</i>

308
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:54,040
<i>Xinzhi.</i>

309
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,840
My kid's only eight.

310
00:21:57,480 --> 00:21:58,560
I really don't want
to jump off a building.

311
00:21:59,400 --> 00:22:02,480
But if you don't save me,
I really will jump.

312
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,720
Are you really going to watch me do it?

313
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:09,720
Xinzhi. I'm begging you.

314
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:12,360
Save me.

315
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:12,200
No need for that. Chi.

316
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:13,480
Can you grab some food?

317
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:15,960
He definitely hasn't been
eating properly lately.

318
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:16,960
He can't even stand straight.

319
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:34,120
HANDMADE EGG ROLL COOKIES

320
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:36,760
If we're talking taste, I'd recommend…

321
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:40,600
This one's got the best flavor.

322
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:42,040
Thanks.

323
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:46,000
Let me introduce myself.

324
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:48,720
I'm Wang Yuan, Woody.

325
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:50,400
An associate partner at C&amp;C.

326
00:23:51,560 --> 00:23:52,960
Hi. I'm Xu Chi.

327
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:56,200
I don't work here. I'm Richard's guest.

328
00:23:56,280 --> 00:23:58,440
I know who you are.
You're one of Maxmise's top people.

329
00:23:59,680 --> 00:24:01,360
Mr. Zheng from Celestial
is an old classmate of mine.

330
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,280
He brings you up all the time.

331
00:24:03,360 --> 00:24:05,320
Always singing your praises.

332
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:14,920
So this is the best we can do?

333
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:16,800
It's the best possible way out

334
00:24:16,880 --> 00:24:18,080
I could offer you.

335
00:24:26,560 --> 00:24:27,480
Thank you.

336
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:40,360
Very well.

337
00:24:42,320 --> 00:24:43,640
Ye Xinzhi.

338
00:24:44,680 --> 00:24:45,520
You're ruthless.

339
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:47,960
Just because I made you
take the fall back then,

340
00:24:48,040 --> 00:24:52,400
you spent ten whole years
scheming to get back at me.

341
00:24:54,360 --> 00:24:55,280
What are you talking about?

342
00:24:56,960 --> 00:24:58,000
Doesn't matter.

343
00:24:58,680 --> 00:25:00,800
You'll end up like me sooner or later.

344
00:25:00,880 --> 00:25:02,560
Publicly vilified.

345
00:25:02,640 --> 00:25:04,120
Scandal everywhere.

346
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,800
You won't escape any of it.

347
00:25:08,040 --> 00:25:09,080
Is that so?

348
00:25:14,320 --> 00:25:16,080
I trained you back then.

349
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:19,040
Now you're training her.

350
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:21,000
You are my payback.

351
00:25:21,800 --> 00:25:24,160
And she is your payback down the road.

352
00:25:26,520 --> 00:25:30,320
Because she is colder than you
and way more ruthless.

353
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:33,000
One day, she'll kick you to the curb

354
00:25:33,080 --> 00:25:35,400
and take your place completely.

355
00:26:09,120 --> 00:26:10,320
Done talking?

356
00:26:17,040 --> 00:26:18,480
I gave him a plan.

357
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:20,720
Things have come to this.

358
00:26:21,720 --> 00:26:25,840
He has to hand over all his shares
per the earn-out agreement.

359
00:26:27,840 --> 00:26:31,600
Eighty percent of the sale proceeds

360
00:26:31,680 --> 00:26:34,160
go to compensating the victims
from Jingshang Department Store

361
00:26:34,240 --> 00:26:36,000
for what they went through.

362
00:26:36,960 --> 00:26:38,360
The remaining 20% covers fines

363
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:42,760
and offsets the losses
of employees and investors.

364
00:26:45,920 --> 00:26:48,440
I also introduced him
to my good friend, lawyer Bai Xiao.

365
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:53,120
If he really has no criminal liability,

366
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:55,600
I'll go talk to Deng

367
00:26:56,360 --> 00:27:00,040
and see if I can get
his industry ban waived.

368
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:02,760
This isn't what you originally planned?

369
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:08,760
Can't just drive him into the ground.

370
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:13,240
I can't exactly

371
00:27:16,480 --> 00:27:17,400
push him to jump, can I?

372
00:27:33,600 --> 00:27:35,520
So what's he got left in the end?

373
00:27:38,240 --> 00:27:40,960
With his drive,
if he looks for the right opening,

374
00:27:41,040 --> 00:27:42,880
he could still make a comeback, I think.

375
00:27:44,360 --> 00:27:45,680
Just like I did back then.

376
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:49,360
But he's getting old.

377
00:27:49,880 --> 00:27:51,880
He doesn't have the edge
you had back then.

378
00:27:56,280 --> 00:27:58,040
Your plan was a complete success.

379
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:01,840
I thought you'd be thrilled.

380
00:28:03,080 --> 00:28:04,560
I thought so too.

381
00:28:05,200 --> 00:28:06,560
Maybe when I saw

382
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:11,200
Yuanzhou's employees
being hauled in for questioning,

383
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:13,760
all of them scared out of their minds…

384
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:17,000
I started to regret it a little.

385
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:21,320
I get it.

386
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:26,920
I don't think I can just
casually comfort you and say,

387
00:28:27,560 --> 00:28:30,800
if they really broke the law,
then getting taken in is only fair.

388
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:34,720
And if they're innocent,
the law will clear their names.

389
00:28:35,960 --> 00:28:38,000
Because I've also been through
a suspension and an investigation.

390
00:28:38,080 --> 00:28:40,840
Back then, I knew I was innocent,

391
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:43,440
but inside, I was still filled
with dread and fear.

392
00:28:47,800 --> 00:28:50,920
And even if they're really fine,

393
00:28:51,640 --> 00:28:53,840
based on how Morse usually handles assets,

394
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:56,640
most of them will still get laid off.

395
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:09,160
We chose this high-risk industry
and took the high pay,

396
00:29:09,240 --> 00:29:11,360
so we should be
mentally prepared for instability.

397
00:29:13,840 --> 00:29:15,160
But we're all human.

398
00:29:15,760 --> 00:29:16,840
We have feelings.

399
00:29:17,360 --> 00:29:18,920
We hurt. We get scared.

400
00:29:27,160 --> 00:29:28,160
Yeah.

401
00:29:31,280 --> 00:29:32,480
Revenge…

402
00:29:34,840 --> 00:29:35,760
isn't exactly a happy thing.

403
00:29:37,960 --> 00:29:39,240
I never thought

404
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:41,520
that hitting a ten-year goal

405
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,680
out of nowhere

406
00:29:46,120 --> 00:29:47,040
would feel like this.

407
00:29:50,640 --> 00:29:52,120
I think I'm suddenly…

408
00:29:55,680 --> 00:29:56,960
a little lost.

409
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:05,000
I think I am too, a bit.

410
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:08,120
The Celestial project is almost over.

411
00:30:10,960 --> 00:30:12,000
What?

412
00:30:13,640 --> 00:30:15,080
Come on, I'll join you for a drink.

413
00:32:20,960 --> 00:32:24,080
To the Celestial Insurance project
wrapping up smoothly. Cheers.

414
00:32:24,160 --> 00:32:25,680
-Cheers.
-Cheers!

415
00:32:29,360 --> 00:32:30,320
Great work this time.

416
00:32:30,400 --> 00:32:32,520
-Thanks for looking out for me.
-Hope we work together again.

417
00:32:33,120 --> 00:32:34,880
‎This one just ended.
‎The next one's about to start.

418
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:36,120
Yes. It's about to start.

419
00:32:38,600 --> 00:32:40,280
-Come on, let's drink.
-Come on.

420
00:32:41,760 --> 00:32:42,760
Come on.

421
00:32:42,840 --> 00:32:43,840
What's wrong?

422
00:32:49,240 --> 00:32:53,760
I just realized this is the first project
we finished at Maxmise.

423
00:32:54,440 --> 00:32:55,280
I'm a little sad to see it end.

424
00:32:57,200 --> 00:32:58,480
Getting sentimental?

425
00:32:59,040 --> 00:33:01,480
It's only the first year.
There are decades ahead.

426
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:02,720
There'll definitely be dozens

427
00:33:02,800 --> 00:33:04,560
or hundreds of even better projects
waiting for us.

428
00:33:05,360 --> 00:33:06,720
Come on.

429
00:33:06,800 --> 00:33:08,880
Our future is gonna be out of this world.

430
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:11,680
-Out of this world.
-Here.

431
00:33:11,760 --> 00:33:13,000
Come on, cheers.

432
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:21,720
Xu Chi.

433
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:25,440
You're on the beach right now. Here.

434
00:33:25,520 --> 00:33:28,360
Take a look. Which of these projects
are you interested in?

435
00:33:28,440 --> 00:33:29,480
Okay.

436
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:36,840
PROJECT PROPOSAL OF ANTAI UNITED INSURANCE

437
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:37,760
PROJECT PROPOSAL OF HUARUI INSURANCE

438
00:33:37,840 --> 00:33:39,920
Why are they all insurance companies?

439
00:33:40,920 --> 00:33:42,320
You just finished the Celestial project.

440
00:33:42,400 --> 00:33:43,800
You know this industry inside out.

441
00:33:45,160 --> 00:33:48,080
Sha Sha's giving you a shot.
You know your stuff.

442
00:33:48,160 --> 00:33:50,280
Once you join the team,
you'll be the go-to person.

443
00:33:50,360 --> 00:33:53,600
After this project,
you'll be set to move up to consultant.

444
00:33:53,680 --> 00:33:57,200
But I don't want to get stuck
bouncing around one industry this early.

445
00:33:57,840 --> 00:33:59,080
Actually, I'm more interested

446
00:33:59,160 --> 00:34:00,800
in the broader space of digital finance.

447
00:34:02,480 --> 00:34:03,600
A lot of the time,

448
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:07,320
your personal interests
and your career path just don't line up.

449
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:10,080
So you have to think it through
and know what to give up.

450
00:34:10,679 --> 00:34:12,120
Isn't there a way to have both?

451
00:34:13,159 --> 00:34:18,239
I hope the company can give me
more say in my own career development.

452
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:19,560
Everyone wants that.

453
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:23,199
If you ever find a company like that,
call me right away.

454
00:34:23,280 --> 00:34:24,320
We'll leave together.

455
00:34:42,159 --> 00:34:43,040
Lin.

456
00:34:43,719 --> 00:34:46,360
I've got another career question.

457
00:34:46,440 --> 00:34:47,920
Can you help me figure it out?

458
00:34:50,440 --> 00:34:51,480
Sure.

459
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:56,600
Ms. Sha.

460
00:34:58,360 --> 00:34:59,400
Come in.

461
00:35:01,640 --> 00:35:03,680
Have you thought it over? Which project?

462
00:35:16,360 --> 00:35:18,600
C&amp;C CONSULTING

463
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:33,720
Mr. Ye.

464
00:35:34,520 --> 00:35:35,840
The files you asked for.

465
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:37,720
-Thanks. Nice work.
-No worries.

466
00:35:37,800 --> 00:35:38,800
You're the one pulling the long hours.

467
00:35:38,880 --> 00:35:40,680
You were in Hong Kong, China,
for a whole week,

468
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:42,200
didn't even go home,
and came straight to the office?

469
00:35:42,280 --> 00:35:44,600
I need to wrap up
what's on my plate first,

470
00:35:44,680 --> 00:35:46,240
then I might take a long break.

471
00:35:47,160 --> 00:35:48,400
What kind of leave?

472
00:35:48,480 --> 00:35:50,400
Don't tell me it's marriage leave?

473
00:35:56,520 --> 00:35:57,360
New hire again?

474
00:35:57,440 --> 00:35:58,800
Yes.

475
00:35:58,880 --> 00:36:02,840
Wang Yuan poached a really sharp girl
to come on as a consultant.

476
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:06,240
<i>Starting today, you're part</i>
<i>of the C&amp;C consulting team.</i>

477
00:36:06,320 --> 00:36:08,280
Welcome to the C&amp;C family.

478
00:36:10,760 --> 00:36:12,560
Great! Welcome!

479
00:36:15,120 --> 00:36:16,320
Alright! Now,

480
00:36:16,400 --> 00:36:18,000
let's keep pushing!

481
00:36:18,080 --> 00:36:19,400
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

482
00:36:23,120 --> 00:36:24,480
Looking forward to working with you.

483
00:36:24,560 --> 00:36:25,960
-Welcome.
-Thank you.

484
00:36:54,080 --> 00:36:54,960
So what's going on?

485
00:36:55,960 --> 00:36:57,360
I wanted to surprise you.

486
00:36:57,440 --> 00:36:58,760
Surprise?

487
00:36:59,600 --> 00:37:01,360
Hi. I'm Xu Chi.

488
00:37:01,440 --> 00:37:02,720
First time here?

489
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:05,600
-Yes.
-What do you think of the place?

490
00:37:06,120 --> 00:37:07,160
It's nice.

491
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:10,440
Just seems a little different
from Maxmise's vibe.

492
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:12,560
I noticed nobody's working late.

493
00:37:13,320 --> 00:37:15,000
We're a local consulting firm.

494
00:37:15,080 --> 00:37:16,880
And these past couple of years,
we've been promoting

495
00:37:16,960 --> 00:37:18,080
a more relaxed way of working.

496
00:37:18,160 --> 00:37:19,720
We encourage working from home.

497
00:37:19,800 --> 00:37:21,440
Plus, with the consultant pool system,

498
00:37:21,520 --> 00:37:23,320
everyone's efficiency has gone way up.

499
00:37:23,400 --> 00:37:25,400
No more trading your health
for your career.

500
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:28,280
-Want some coffee?
-No thanks.

501
00:37:28,800 --> 00:37:32,000
What's this consultant pool system
you mentioned?

502
00:37:32,080 --> 00:37:34,920
It's a management system derived
from the lawyer pool model.

503
00:37:37,200 --> 00:37:38,880
How do I put this?

504
00:37:39,480 --> 00:37:43,760
Traditional consulting firms
are all team-based, right?

505
00:37:45,280 --> 00:37:49,480
Junior consultants
can only follow a fixed partner team.

506
00:37:49,560 --> 00:37:52,520
So the work they're exposed to
is pretty narrow.

507
00:37:52,600 --> 00:37:54,080
But with a consultant pool,
it's different.

508
00:37:54,160 --> 00:37:57,680
Even young consultants
can work on individual projects

509
00:37:57,760 --> 00:38:00,880
and communicate both ways
with different teams.

510
00:38:01,480 --> 00:38:03,160
That way, young consultants

511
00:38:03,240 --> 00:38:07,360
can quickly find
their own lane and domain.

512
00:38:07,440 --> 00:38:10,120
And there's less friction between teams.

513
00:38:11,880 --> 00:38:13,480
So? Interested in giving it a shot?

514
00:38:18,600 --> 00:38:20,960
Are you poaching me?

515
00:38:22,960 --> 00:38:27,720
Actually, people move
between consulting firms all the time.

516
00:38:27,800 --> 00:38:30,880
Besides, my team
is always hungry for talent.

517
00:38:32,600 --> 00:38:33,960
Thanks so much.

518
00:38:35,040 --> 00:38:36,400
But I'm doing pretty well at Maxmise.

519
00:38:37,920 --> 00:38:39,240
Plus,

520
00:38:40,080 --> 00:38:42,120
I'm actually Richard's girlfriend.

521
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:44,880
So even if I were going to jump ship, I…

522
00:38:46,480 --> 00:38:48,720
But Richard is on another project,

523
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,720
and his team is already full.

524
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:57,480
Let me share a personal experience.

525
00:38:57,560 --> 00:39:02,760
Most of the time, people don't jump ship
because they can't hack it where they are.

526
00:39:02,840 --> 00:39:05,520
It's because a wise person
knows which ship to board.

527
00:39:07,160 --> 00:39:09,320
You're still an SBA at Maxmise, right?

528
00:39:11,560 --> 00:39:13,240
Here's the thing. Come work with me.

529
00:39:13,320 --> 00:39:15,160
I'll give you a consultant title.

530
00:39:15,240 --> 00:39:16,680
Once the next project wraps up,

531
00:39:16,760 --> 00:39:19,360
I'll recommend you for project manager.

532
00:39:21,880 --> 00:39:22,960
That's really tempting.

533
00:39:24,120 --> 00:39:25,360
But still, thank you.

534
00:39:26,000 --> 00:39:26,840
No problem.

535
00:39:27,520 --> 00:39:28,560
Think it over.

536
00:39:34,200 --> 00:39:35,280
Here's my card.

537
00:39:36,520 --> 00:39:38,680
-Thanks.
-Great running into you here.

538
00:39:39,840 --> 00:39:41,640
That day you said here

539
00:39:41,720 --> 00:39:44,560
that suddenly hitting your goal
felt like losing your direction.

540
00:39:45,560 --> 00:39:46,680
Honestly, me too.

541
00:39:47,280 --> 00:39:50,440
I've been at Maxmise for over a year
and finished two projects.

542
00:39:50,520 --> 00:39:52,200
I've learned so much.

543
00:39:52,280 --> 00:39:54,440
By all logic, I should feel satisfied.

544
00:39:54,520 --> 00:39:56,400
But I keep remembering
what you told me that day.

545
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:59,280
You said work shouldn't be our whole life,

546
00:40:00,080 --> 00:40:02,840
and we should spend more time
together going forward.

547
00:40:03,440 --> 00:40:05,080
But if I stay at Maxmise,

548
00:40:05,160 --> 00:40:08,240
it's really hard to do that
and still keep up my pace of promotions.

549
00:40:08,320 --> 00:40:10,000
You know how it is.

550
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:11,360
My track record at Maxmise right now

551
00:40:11,440 --> 00:40:12,880
is mostly the result of me
grinding myself to the bone.

552
00:40:15,040 --> 00:40:18,320
So when Wang Yuan
promised you a consultant title,

553
00:40:18,920 --> 00:40:20,240
you were tempted?

554
00:40:22,680 --> 00:40:25,120
The higher you go,
the harder it is to move up.

555
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:28,400
It took Lin a full five years
to become a consultant.

556
00:40:29,240 --> 00:40:30,920
I don't want to waste that much time,

557
00:40:31,440 --> 00:40:33,400
and I don't want to be stuck
in the same pigeonhole forever.

558
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:35,760
But C&amp;C's consultant pool

559
00:40:35,840 --> 00:40:38,360
gives me way more flexibility
to pick projects that actually fit me.

560
00:40:39,360 --> 00:40:42,120
Lin and Tianna both told me
to grab this opportunity.

561
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:44,040
Xinzhi,

562
00:40:44,120 --> 00:40:46,880
I really do want to have
more time with you.

563
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:50,160
Now that you're coming to work with me,
of course, I'm happy.

564
00:40:51,520 --> 00:40:55,320
But it would've been better
if you'd given me a heads-up.

565
00:40:56,000 --> 00:40:58,960
After all, I know C&amp;C better than you do.

566
00:40:59,720 --> 00:41:01,320
-I…
-Let me go pour you some tea.

567
00:41:04,040 --> 00:41:06,720
I wanted to tell you,

568
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:09,440
but you were traveling nonstop
for a while there.

569
00:41:09,520 --> 00:41:12,440
And my second and third interviews
didn't go that great.

570
00:41:12,520 --> 00:41:13,640
So I was even more scared to tell you.

571
00:41:13,720 --> 00:41:16,080
What if I got cut?
That'd be so embarrassing.

572
00:41:16,160 --> 00:41:19,000
Good thing I ended up getting the offer.

573
00:41:20,440 --> 00:41:22,040
Just to be clear upfront.

574
00:41:22,120 --> 00:41:25,840
I don't want people gossiping
that I only got in because of you.

575
00:41:27,320 --> 00:41:29,640
So don't put me on your team yet.

576
00:41:30,240 --> 00:41:32,040
Let me work a project or two
with other teams

577
00:41:32,120 --> 00:41:34,000
in the consultant pool
and become a veteran.

578
00:41:34,080 --> 00:41:36,560
Have you gotten addicted
to going undercover?

579
00:41:37,200 --> 00:41:39,520
Our relationship is not exactly a secret.

580
00:41:40,120 --> 00:41:41,800
I was gonna talk to you about it.

581
00:41:41,880 --> 00:41:44,040
Once I get through this busy stretch,
let's go on a trip.

582
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:47,840
I'm in no mood for a trip right now.

583
00:41:54,520 --> 00:41:55,520
Here's what I'm thinking.

584
00:41:56,640 --> 00:42:01,160
Well, career-wise,
I want people to see us as,

585
00:42:01,240 --> 00:42:03,160
not exactly equals,

586
00:42:03,240 --> 00:42:04,760
but at least not too far apart in rank.

587
00:42:05,640 --> 00:42:08,240
Once I finish two projects,
I'll definitely make project manager.

588
00:42:08,320 --> 00:42:11,560
And even if some people
in the industry know about us,

589
00:42:11,640 --> 00:42:13,240
hardly anyone at the company does.

590
00:42:13,840 --> 00:42:16,960
So I don't want to broadcast it.

591
00:42:17,040 --> 00:42:20,680
At least not until everyone here
actually recognizes what I can do.

592
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:25,280
Just wait for me. Please?

593
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:28,120
Okay.

594
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:34,080
Miss Xu, on behalf of C&amp;C, welcome.

595
00:42:40,720 --> 00:42:43,560
Now we can commute,

596
00:42:43,640 --> 00:42:45,640
travel for work, and go home together.

597
00:42:54,880 --> 00:42:56,720
So don't be mad at me anymore.

598
00:42:57,280 --> 00:42:58,120
I'm not mad.

599
00:42:59,320 --> 00:43:00,520
You really aren't?

600
00:43:01,760 --> 00:43:02,760
Really?

601
00:43:08,320 --> 00:43:10,200
-Then I'm heading out to work.
-Go on.

602
00:43:18,840 --> 00:43:22,920
"Honey, we can commute,

603
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:25,320
travel for work, and go home together."

604
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:26,680
"Alright?"

605
00:43:26,760 --> 00:43:28,200
-Are you out of your mind?
-You're such a menace.

606
00:43:29,080 --> 00:43:30,840
You… Wait.

607
00:43:30,920 --> 00:43:35,440
So you mean
you have to keep it low-key at work,

608
00:43:35,520 --> 00:43:38,400
sneak around with an office romance,

609
00:43:38,480 --> 00:43:40,440
and hide it all from your colleagues?

610
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:45,800
Nice.

611
00:43:45,880 --> 00:43:47,360
Now the tables have turned.

612
00:43:47,440 --> 00:43:48,480
So you're in charge now.

613
00:43:50,080 --> 00:43:51,720
That's called adding some spice.

614
00:43:53,120 --> 00:43:54,280
Spice.

615
00:43:54,360 --> 00:43:56,920
Didn't you and Zhao Heng
used to be like this?

616
00:43:59,200 --> 00:44:01,480
I don't really get
this "spice" thing of yours.

617
00:44:01,560 --> 00:44:02,600
Me and Zhao Heng…

618
00:44:02,680 --> 00:44:05,760
He completely dances to my tune. Okay?

619
00:44:05,840 --> 00:44:07,280
Can't say the same for you
and Ye Xinzhi, though.

620
00:44:08,400 --> 00:44:10,240
Who says? Ye Xinzhi treats me great.

621
00:44:10,320 --> 00:44:12,440
Way better than Zhao Heng treats you.

622
00:44:14,920 --> 00:44:16,480
Zhao Heng treats me pretty well.

623
00:44:18,440 --> 00:44:22,760
But honestly, after you left Maxmise,
I've been thinking about quitting too.

624
00:44:23,880 --> 00:44:24,760
Go back to your dad's company?

625
00:44:27,240 --> 00:44:28,880
Though my family
has accepted Zhao Heng now,

626
00:44:28,960 --> 00:44:31,080
I'm still not sure deep down.

627
00:44:31,160 --> 00:44:35,080
I figure it might be better
if I go work at my dad's company.

628
00:44:35,680 --> 00:44:37,920
Once I'm settled,
Zhao Heng can come help me

629
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:40,080
or stay in consulting.

630
00:44:40,160 --> 00:44:42,120
Either way, I've got options.

631
00:44:42,200 --> 00:44:43,440
So you're not gonna be a partner?

632
00:44:44,160 --> 00:44:47,880
Ever since I met you,
becoming a partner was your big dream.

633
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:52,520
Girl, running Siwei Group
and being a partner at Maxmise

634
00:44:52,600 --> 00:44:54,960
aren't even in the same league. Okay?

635
00:44:55,040 --> 00:44:56,480
That's not what you used to say.

636
00:44:57,360 --> 00:44:59,200
I get it now. It's the magic of love.

637
00:44:59,280 --> 00:45:01,600
Does Zhao Heng know
you're doing all this for him?

638
00:45:01,680 --> 00:45:04,080
Well, I… I…

639
00:45:04,160 --> 00:45:09,480
I'm going back to Siwei Group
to take back my spot as the heiress.

640
00:45:09,560 --> 00:45:11,720
He's just playing a supporting role.
He doesn't need to know all this.

641
00:45:13,440 --> 00:45:15,640
I get it. He's Bu Shoes-On.

642
00:45:15,720 --> 00:45:17,240
I'm Shoes-Off.

643
00:45:18,240 --> 00:45:21,520
Hey, I gotta say, you're such a menace,

644
00:45:21,600 --> 00:45:24,360
-I swear.
-Who are you calling a menace?

645
00:45:25,440 --> 00:45:26,800
B.t let me warn you,

646
00:45:26,880 --> 00:45:30,120
If you go back and your dad sticks you
in some department with a fancy name,

647
00:45:30,200 --> 00:45:33,640
like PR or venture capital, don't take it.

648
00:45:33,720 --> 00:45:37,160
Go for the departments that actually
control the company's core business.

649
00:45:38,280 --> 00:45:40,480
Don't worry. I know what I'm doing.

650
00:45:40,560 --> 00:45:41,880
-That's good then.
-There's a vacancy

651
00:45:41,960 --> 00:45:43,320
for a manager at the Finance Center.

652
00:45:43,400 --> 00:45:44,680
I'll go fill that spot first.

653
00:45:45,480 --> 00:45:47,800
With my experience
from the Celestial Insurance project,

654
00:45:47,880 --> 00:45:50,040
I should be able to handle it.
Should be fine.

655
00:45:50,640 --> 00:45:51,440
Good.
